<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Config",
    subtitle: "Configure the host-owned user contract, layout, mounted paths, and editable profile fields.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Pre-route configuration",
    subtitle: "Set route values before the host draws the mount and engine routes.",
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    language: :ruby,
    code: <<~'CODE'
      # config/routes.rb, before the mount declaration
      RecordingStudioUser.configure do |config|
        config.mount_path = "/account"
        config.profile_route_path = "settings/profile"
        config.admin_route_path = "reporting/users"
      end

      mount RecordingStudioUser::Engine => RecordingStudioUser.config.mount_path,
            as: :recording_studio_users
    CODE
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Normal initializer configuration",
    subtitle: "These settings do not change routes that the host has already drawn.",
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    language: :ruby,
    code: <<~'CODE'
      # config/initializers/recording_studio_user.rb
      RecordingStudioUser.configure do |config|
        config.user_class_name = "User"
        config.layout = "application"
        config.additional_profile_attributes = %i[display_name]
        config.require_password_confirmation = false
        # config.login_title = "Welcome back"
        config.omniauth_providers = {
          google_oauth2: {
            client_id: ENV.fetch("GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID", "test-google-client-id"),
            client_secret: ENV.fetch("GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET", "test-google-client-secret")
          }
        }
        config.omniauth_create_account = true
      end
    CODE
  ) %>

  <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-(--surface-content-color)">
    Defaults are <code>User</code>, <code>application</code>, <code>/recording_studio_users</code>,
    <code>profile</code>, and <code>admin</code>. A conventional initializer runs too late to change an already
    mounted engine path or its already-drawn profile and admin routes.
    <code>omniauth_providers</code> defaults to an empty hash (no Continue buttons). Keys may include
    <code>google_oauth2</code>, <code>microsoft_graph</code>, <code>apple</code>, <code>linkedin</code>, and
    <code>instagram</code>.
    <code>omniauth_create_account</code> defaults to <code>true</code>.
    <code>login_title</code> defaults to <code>Welcome back</code> for the Devise login heading.
    Host Devise must route OmniAuth callbacks to
    <code>recording_studio_user/omniauth_callbacks</code> when providers are configured.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-(--surface-content-color)">
    Mount paths gain one leading slash and omit a trailing slash. Profile and admin paths omit both leading and
    trailing slashes. Paths must be non-empty, contain only letters, numbers, underscores, slashes, and hyphens,
    and cannot contain a double slash.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-(--surface-content-color)">
    The configured <code>user_class_name</code> must name the host's existing Devise-compatible Active Record model
    returned by <code>current_user</code>. It must use the host UUID primary key and expose <code>email</code>
    and timestamps. Name, time zone, and extra profile fields live on Profile under the shared People root.
    Additional profile attributes are allowlisted explicitly; identity, credential, authorization, membership, root,
    recording, and recordable fields are protected and cannot be configured for profile updates.
  </p>
</div>
